WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
<b>Drawing Fun!</b>

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:02.400
Drawing!

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.560
F - U - N !

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.080
Miss Kisaragi, Miss Kisaragi!

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.560
What's up Suneko-san?

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.560
I decided to take up Art Design, today!

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.960
Sketchbook

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.690
That's wonderful!

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.410
Oh! But I don't know how to draw!

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.050
Oh my!

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.550
What do I do? What do I do?

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.550
Well then! Why don't we take a look

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.460
at what "GA" is up to?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.660
Gee eh?

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.070
Geijutsuka Art Design Class!

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.360
And so...!

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.580
GA: Geijutsuka Art Design Class...

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.030
is about to begin!

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.930
This was the introduction.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:54.850
"GA!"

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.290
GA's morning greeting.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.850
GA!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.280
Yamaguchi, was it?

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.260
What are you doing over there?

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.180
It just seemed so wasteful.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.700
So I picked them up.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:16.790
What?

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.310
Cherry blossoms that have just bloomed.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.280
Hurry!

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.520
First bell.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:34.780
You forgot...

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.210
Your bag.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.300
Th-Thank you.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.090
Waa! I'm gonna be late!

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:44.880
Huh?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.350
Why is everyone standing around?

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.230
No reason.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.630
Let's go.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.430
Okay!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:50.320
Second bell.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.120
Like I'd lose!

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:08.510
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:28.050
<b>Drawing Fun</b>

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.070
GA: Geijutsuka Art Design Class.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.130
A class that focuses on Visual, Textile,
and related design fields.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.640
Because of this,
 there are a lot of people here

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.700
with original styles.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.690
In their fashion, for example.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.940
For better or worse.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.740
That's right!
 For those who study design

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.800
it's natural to pursue 
originality of expression.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.660
So! We've redesigned the 
school's athletic uniform!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.420
This is it!

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.820
That's clearly a violation of school rules!

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.780
Rest assured! We've redesigned the interior.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.170
And by reversing it... look!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.340
Like Edo city residents
when luxury goods were prohibited.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.220
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.350
Of course, at GA

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.460
we also study art and design techniques.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.960
Squish

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.710
Oh no. It's sort of mixing 
with the undercoat.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.140
Oh, Kisaragi-dono,

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.550
poster paints aren't designed for layering

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.090
and will mix if overlapped.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.140
I thought poster paints were water-resistant?

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.560
Actually, they're water-soluble.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.500
They use pigments, however, 
so the color is vivid.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.740
Then I guess they can't be 
used on cellophane or fabric.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.980
Whoo. It's hot.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.490
<b>Relief</b>

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.990
There's mold in my paint.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.910
Even though I only used it once.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:45.730
Woe...

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.540
Blue-green and orange poster paint mold

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.500
particularly easily, don't they?

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.230
Okay! I'll remove the mold from your paint!

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.540
Super-Effective... Noda-chan-Aura!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.010
Noda-chan Aura?!

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.120
You may rest assured.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.300
I've infused this poster 
paint with Noda-chan energy.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.690
And by doing this...?

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.000
The sun-like Noda-chan Aura eliminates

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.970
all traces of even the most stubborn mold.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.260
Oooh! Amazing!

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:16.300
Sketch Mars' bust in 5 seconds starting now!

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.190
Impossible

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.500
<b> 1 Week Later</b>

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:24.740
Poof

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.020
I don't know why you'd expect anything else.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:24.740
Close the lid gently!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.090
Ah! It's all hard.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.660
Oh that poster paint is old 
 so just clean it out.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:33.680
Okay.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.160
Hey, hey. Noda-chan, look.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.450
If I paint some brown on top...

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.860
Oo! Pudding!

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.800
Squeezing some white paint 
for whipped cream...

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.970
Make some cherries and chocolate

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:54.930
and flakes out of paper...

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.630
Instantly: a la mode!

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:59.480
Let's put more cream on it!

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.550
Hey, you two.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.780
I know it's fun to fool around
but we're in a painting class, so paint.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.880
Make some eraser shavings.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.230
Then gather it up.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.600
Mix it with some paste.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.100
Color it with some paint or crayon.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.610
And it's ready!

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.710
Ooh! Homemade kneaded erasers!

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:22.950
This is so nostalgic.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.400
Like from elementary school!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.400
It doesn't have any smell though.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.210
It can't really erase anything either.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:30.310
Hey you three.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.980
I know it’s fun to fool around but we're-

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.670
<b>Grrrrr </b>

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.050
I wouldn't.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:34.670
You'll turn into one of them.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.040
Design means (probably) 
individuality and uniqueness!!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:44.820
<b>Swoosh swoosh swoosh...</b>

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.250
AIDMA law, color composition and placement...

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.810
ignore all of it!

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.410
I don't think you should ignore all--

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.420
Move your brush with inspiration!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.070
I-It wasn't on purpose!

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.380
It was an accident!

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.280
You made her cry, you made her cry.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.230
Idiot! No I didn't! Yet! Shut up, Noda!

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.560
Don't worry about it! It's fine!

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.470
Hey, I bet you could paint an
even better one than before!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.410
Don't cry! Don’t cry!

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.130
I'll buy you some candy, okay?

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:20.030
I can't tell if Tomokane 
is manly or just mean.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.040
Start by apologizing.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.400
I'm sorry.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:29.500
Tomokane! What do we have next?

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:32.410
One sec. It's... Ski...?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.000
Textiles     Sketching     Fine Arts

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:34.000
Scr...

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:35.790
Scratch Cats!

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.520
You mean Sketching.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.260
If it's Sketching, then that probably
means we’ll be drawing.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.170
I'll need my pencils and my sketchbook...

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.850
Do we need our rough sketchbook?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.490
We don't.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.960
Art Room 1

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.620
Let's go early and grab the 
window seats by the back.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.180
Okay. Let's go!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.040
Window seats are the best.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.360
Hey. We're leaving, Kisaragi.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:58.890
Kisaragi?

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.970
What's wrong?

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.870
Right. What were we talking about?

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:08.160
Kisaragi-chan was fantasizing about Scratch Cats.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.530
How did you know?!

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.860
That one would also be an example, right?

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:16.550
Yes.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.180
There are many different 
kinds even on campus.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:19.960
Yes.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:23.370
Kisaragi-chan, what are you doing?

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.050
Pictogram hunting, apparently.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.740
Preparation for today's design class.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.640
Kisaragi-dono, here as well.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.210
What are pictograms?

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:36.360
Design Assignment: Original 
Pictogram. Size: A4

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:35.790
Pictograms are a type of modern day visual symbol.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:40.660
There are many types, including signs
in public spaces and computer icons.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.530
Even company brand logos?

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:45.150
Those are monograms:
 symbols made from letters.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.680
Pictograms are, like their 
name implies, from pictures.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:50.470
Well then, what are anagrams?

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.630
That's a type of wordplay where you
rearrange the letters in a word.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.480
<b>No da mi ki</b>

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.250
If you rearrange the 
letters in Nodamiki...

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:56.810
<b>mi ki</b>

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:03.990
<b>Ki no mi da
(It's a nut!)</b>

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.500
You get Kinomida!

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.000
Oh! I get it!

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.990
And Namiko-san, you're how many kilograms?

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.880
Oh well let's see...

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:06.990
Wait! That was close.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:10.420
I was about to say it.

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:12.860
Pictograms vary greatly,

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.760
depending on the information
  or instruction implied.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:20.250
For example, using this typical
 human pictogram as a reference...

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:23.330
By changing the shape, motif, or color...

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.880
Wow! They take on different 
ages and genders!

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.470
Well then, can we make 
pictograms of specific people?

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.550
<b>Tomokane-san</b>

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:36.590
<b> Noda-chan</b>

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:34.050
With that much detail,
 it's just a painting.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.380
It has to be more symbolic.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.580
Done!

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:39.650
A pictogram of Kisaragi-chan.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:40.910
Mine is Namiko-san.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.800
I wonder why...

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:45.940
I feel like I can imagine what it 
might look like before I even see it.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.640
I haven't seen mine either,

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.130
<b>Yahoo!</b>

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.340
but for some reason I feel like punching her.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.370
Tomokane is like this!

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.220
Noda is like this!

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.220
As you can see,

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.010
when a person has a 
recognizable characteristic

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.110
this is a simple matter.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.420
Let's take Sotoma-sensei as an example.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.920
Everyone, make sure you hand in your

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.500
What would you to draw?

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:05.800
assignments before the end of the day.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.250
Hmm...

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.120
<b>Skritch, skritch...</b>

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:06.860
Got it?

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.450
I get this kind of impression.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.220
This would be an example 
taking teacher as a motif.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:15.220
I think it would be like this.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.560
This would be an example taking 
a daily scene as a motif.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:15.660
 Motif

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.560
 Motif

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.330
As an opposite approach...

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:25.040
Drink       Take Medicine      Bedroom

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.240
First we can take a set of arbitrary words

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.210
and then create pictograms

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.320
from the images they represent.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.990
Oh, so that's how it turns out.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.940
Let's try it, Tomokane-dono.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:36.080
Construction Site   Shower    Baseball

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:30.770
Okay!

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:33.520
Like this?

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.520
What is this, "spot the difference"?

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.690
As a hint you can use these.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.820
So, these are considered pictograms as well.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.040
Traffic signs are generally 
congruous around the world.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.420
Congested, indeed.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.730
Congruous <-> Congested

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.660
Wow...

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.140
You called?

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.170
<b> Warning:  Slippery</b>

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.170
No I didn't! My bad, okay?

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:58.130
Wow!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:02.160
A diagonal line means prohibited, right?

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:02.840
Right, right.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:04.200
I'm sure you've seen

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.220
‘no smoking’ or 
‘no cell phone usage’ signs.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.870
This one is for 
‘no (inappropriate) touching’.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.730
and this is for ‘no eloping’.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:12.640
Really...

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.330
You mustn’t believe everything you hear.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:18.080
I can't get past it!

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:21.840
<b> Dangerous Goods Prohibited</b>

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.540
For some reason I can't go any further!

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.000
It looks like these yellow triangular signs

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.360
are used to indicate caution.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:30.690
In one way or another, they 
all seem rather painful.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.520
I sure feel bad for Pictoman.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.000
<b>Right?</b>

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.200
Pictoman?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.740
Ahh, I see.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:37.750
That's why he wants to escape.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.110
Hey hey, Noda-chan.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.020
What's this pictogram mean?

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.080
I think that...

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:50.490
That's a sign for Public Evacuation Shelter.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.520
That's why!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.190
Kyouju, what's that?

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.350
I tried placing a number of pictograms

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:59.330
of various genres randomly on my desk.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:01.600
I choose some at random and create

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.570
a new pictogram by combining them.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:05.040
Then, here!

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.570
Take these two and try 
making a new pictogram.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:09.770
Let's see...

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.430
Maybe like this?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.170
I thought of this right away!

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.240
Really? It isn't more like this?

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.790
What is that monster?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:21.100
This sure does reveal a 
lot about each person.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.300
Then how about you, Namiko-san?

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.090
I've already done mine.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.120
You know those recycling bins outside?

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.380
All different kinds of

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.780
trash seem to get mixed together, right?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.600
I really wanted to find a 
way to keep it organized.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.480
So I used this daily 
experience as inspiration

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:40.300
and created different 
pictograms for each bin.

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:41.930
Bottles, cans, plastic 
bottles, recyclable paper,

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.100
recyclable plastic, combustible 
trash, incombustible trash...

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.110
These are all for your assignment?

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.620
Have you decided on something, Kisaragi?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.350
Oh yes!

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.280
Behind this building there's

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:54.520
this place that gets a lot of sunlight.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.980
Sometimes I find cats gathering there.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.360
Really.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:05.260
Cat Appearance Area

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:03.890
I feel like she might draw 
this kind of pictogram.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:18.040
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.670
Instantly, A la mode!

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.170
Is today's rough sketch in charcoal?

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.450
Yes! We'll need charcoal and an easel.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.380
And we'll need mayonnaise too!

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:25.510
Mayonnaise?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.200
To put on the bread crusts and eat.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.950
Bread crusts are used as erasers for charcoal sketching.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.950
<b>Yum yum</b>

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.460
Who uses mayonnaise on bread crusts?!

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:33.240
Tomokane-san!

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.290
You're correcting her on the wrong point!

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:43.300
Oh, what should I do?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.750
I just can't seem to 
start my art assignment!

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.450
What seems to be the problem?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.510
Who are you guys?

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.030
If you have assignment 
problems, leave it to us!

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:56.150
I'm the captain, Rough Sketch Red!

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:57.580
Technique Yellow!

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:58.870
Coloring Magenta!

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.670
Effective Cyan!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:01.650
Corrective Monochrome.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:04.150
<b>Whoosh!</b>

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.780
We will dye it!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.170
Subtractive Mixture Colors!

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:07.690
Color Warriors! Irodo Rangers!

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:07.960
<b>Color Warriors   Irodo Rangers</b>

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:08.550
Naming fail.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:10.990
Here we go!

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:25.180
<b>Grumble grumble</b>

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:12.990
Black and white are achromatic.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.530
You're in CMYK so it's probably fine.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.930
More importantly, who would 
make the leader red?

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:20.090
Cat ears...

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.000
What?!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.420
Our coordination is in 
shambles from the start.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.180
Let's go, Irodo Rangers!

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.440
Our opponent today is… this guy!

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:29.680
<b>Assignment     Art Class. (No Theme)
 TYPE - B2 Print</b>

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.830
Get ready and let’s finish it!

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:29.680
Yeah!

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:31.180
To start with...

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.450
Red will...

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.750
kinda like this...

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:35.420
Design!

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:36.770
We're going with this!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:37.670
Go!

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.270
Wow. This is kinda lame.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:39.690
Go!

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.430
But it's Captain's orders...

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:42.900
Once the sketch is done,

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.290
get started on the undercoat right away!

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:45.330
Go, Magenta!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.100
Roger!

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.230
Complete!

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:50.120
All right!

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.400
Next is...

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.940
<b>Stop</b>

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.260
We can't do anything until it dries...

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:00.110
1 hour later

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:00.800
Irodo Rangers!

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.210
<b>Color Warriors
 Irodo Rangers</b>

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.520
All right. It should be done by now!

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:02.890
Go!

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.240
Next are Yellow and Cyan!

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:05.450
Right!

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:05.450
Right!

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.440
All right. Masking complete!

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:12.490
It's ready to go, Cyan!

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:13.640
Oh, Okay!

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.060
Then with my spattering...

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.370
Spattering?!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.880
That's so cheap!

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.750
We're not in elementary school anymore!

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:22.570
<b>Waaaah</b>

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:22.280
What can I do?

00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:23.830
Airbrushes are so expensive!

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:24.740
Oh well, I guess.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:26.520
Don't use too much paint 
and be careful, all right?

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:27.430
Or else we'll get bubbles.

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.310
Oh well, I guess.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:28.740
Okay.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:31.980
And, there!

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:34.770
I've finished!

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.580
<b>Ta-da!</b>

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:37.110
Ooh! Gradation, right?

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:42.220
<b>Drip drip</b>

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.350
Huh? What!

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.220
The paint's dripping.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:45.410
Oh! I painted on the 
undercoat without thinning it,

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:49.560
Undiluted!!

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:47.610
so it takes longer to dry!

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.560
Thin your poster colors with 
water before painting!

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.460
<b>Sooo sad</b>

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.680
Oh no! Even the tape is sticking!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:55.880
GA is ruined!

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.210
What do we do, Red?

00:15:57.210 --> 00:16:00.670
Seems like everything 
is out of control, Red!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.210
Final Attack!

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.760
It's kind of unique, right?!

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:13.420
That's what you always say when you mess up.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:14.050
<b>Mhmm</b>

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.100
Shit. Then it's time for our trump card.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.690
We're counting on you, Monochrome!

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:22.740
Understood.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:23.430
<b>Safety First</b>

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:23.430
Plunk

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:27.000
<b>*Sad sigh*</b>

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:27.700
<b>Thwunk</b>

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.400
White Out     Pretend it never happened.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.810
White Out       Pretend it never happened.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.810
...is about as far as I thought.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:44.210
<b>Skritch, skritch...</b>

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:38.140
It's not like the assignment 
would just disappear,

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.550
even if we painted over it.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:42.850
Good for nothing Color Warriors.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.320
<b>Technical University 
Ayanoii High School</b>

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:49.460
Morning, Kyouju!

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.320
Yes.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.080
I'll take over.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.830
Oh! Thanks, Kyouju-san.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:02.040
Shoot! I forgot tape for varnishing.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.130
Kyouju, you don't have any, do you?

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.470
It's something like that.

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:07.380
Like that?

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.630
Is it like that?

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:11.380
Masa, about this color textbook...

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:10.670
Masa?!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:15.520
Next is Art Room 2.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.180
<b>Poink</b>

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.400
What are you doing, Noda?

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:20.460
When you see little corners like this,

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:22.050
don't you just want to squeeze into them?

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:23.050
It's relaxing!

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:23.930
I'll go ahead.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.170
I'll take out the trash.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:31.350
Oh! Thank you, Kyouju-san.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.490
Have fun!

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:39.740
<b>Poink</b>

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.610
Visible Light

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:44.610
I will begin our lecture on Color.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.300
Let us suppose we have two apples here.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:51.620
There are both red and blue apples.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:55.120
Then why does this apple appear red?

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.990
Kisaragi-dono, do you know?

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:58.170
Ah, yes!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:01.360
Uhm... uhm... the reason 
why apples appear red

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:03.150
is because the tree fairy

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:06.080
painted them with red paint?

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.260
Is she a natural airhead?

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:09.210
Is she an idiot? 
Should I cut in?

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.800
That's not it, Kisaragi-chan.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.590
Normally, you might think that color

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:15.310
is attached to the apple.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:16.680
But really, it's over here,

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:20.040
the human eye is what picks up the red light.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.910
The light that shows you the color

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:23.780
Visible Light

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.780
is known as 'visible light'.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:26.030
In other words, though the human eye

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.990
perceives light like this...

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.970
Animals, like dogs, see it like this...

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.490
And aliens might see it like this.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:40.050
Today, we explore computer graphics

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.420
for the first time!

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.650
What's that?

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:47.970
Is that where you use a computer
to draw pictures and make designs?

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:50.080
This is the first time I've gone to class

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:51.310
without having to bring painting tools!

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.200
CG...

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.400
This really feels like we're
 studying to be professionals, right?

00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:00.430
With this we'll be able to 
make Hollywood movies, huh!

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:01.700
Huh?!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:02.920
Hollywood movies?

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:13.770
Getting to the classroom is
a lot more work than I thought.

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:17.100
Well, the computer lab is in the university building...

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.000
Look, technical university students.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.640
They were looking at me, weren't they?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.060
Did they fall for me?

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.910
Nah. It's probably the uniform.

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.140
Yaaah! It's far!

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.420
Thirty seconds until the chime.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.490
At the end of the second floor 
to the right is the computer lab.

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:36.250
All right!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.360
Let's hurry!

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.160
What's the matter, Noda?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.370
What's the matter, Noda?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.690
Maybe Noda-chan should
be on stand-by after school.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:47.530
In case those guys come back to pick me up.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:49.170
Then just wait here.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.400
<b> Computer Lab</b>

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.400
First, we'll need to practice 
getting used to it!

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.250
Use the tools on the top left

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.140
to make a simple drawing.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:00.700
Oh! I wonder what- 
I made something!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.420
This isn't what I wanted to do!

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.290
Once you've finished we're to print it out

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:10.440
and submit it.

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:12.060
Masa, you're so fast.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.290
Are you done, Kisaragi?

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:18.230
While I was using the 
tool shape I somehow...

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:19.930
This is a little Noda-esque, isn't it?

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:20.700
Kisaragi-chan!

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:21.260
Oh, the real one appeared.

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.390
How's your computer debut?

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:24.430
It was way over my head!

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.720
But with computers you can
redo it as many times as you want.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.410
It sure is hassle-free and useful.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.260
Besides, Noda can't pull any tricks

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:33.960
like mixing your paints
 behind your back.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:35.410
You're right!

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:38.530
Or Tomokane destroying your work.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.920
You're absolutely right.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.420
<b> The Next Week</b>

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.010
Huh?

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.330
What's the matter, Noda-dono?

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:48.380
My files from last week aren't anywhere!

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:49.490
The computers here are used by

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:52.430
all the middle, high school, 
and university students.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:54.950
There are cases where user’s 
data has been erased.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:55.670
Darn.

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:58.400
Were Kisaragi's files deleted too?

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:01.590
This looks like Noda-chan's work...

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:08.410
Hey, wasn't the pictogram 
assignment due today?!

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:09.690
I handed it in!

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:10.600
Handed in ages ago.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.200
Already turned it in.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.100
Seriously?

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:16.120
Ahhh! What do I do?!

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:17.090
<b>Panic!</b>

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.250
Hurry up and do it already.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.180
Since it's come to this, I'm leaving 
it up to the god of randomness!

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:20.940
C'mon cards!

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:22.070
Don't cheat.

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:23.220
This and this and this!

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:25.280
That's a challenge.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.480
I have to do it!

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:28.430
Done!

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:30.170
I'm gonna hand it in!

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:36.510
Are those the pictogram assignments?

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:37.310
Yes.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:41.460
Baby Car

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:44.730
Caution: Heartthrob

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:47.740
Misleading

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.810
Rebellious Age! Let's stop cautioning him.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.730
They have potential.

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:54.210
But no practical use.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode:</b>

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:28.670
Scratch Cats has a nice feeling to it, right?

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:32.290
Without decoration, a cat lives
 naturally and scratches trees.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:34.420
Kisaragi-chan is daydreaming,

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:35.550
but it's time for the
 next episode preview.

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:37.310
Let's close in on the secrets of GA.

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:40.060
The Divine Pencil

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:39.040
Were there any secrets to begin with?
